      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, I'm here because... for almost two years now, I've just had this absolute certainty that ever since that big commission, a few people in my ensemble have been quietly trying to undermine my work. They do it through, you know, sudden schedule changes, or how they choose their seating, or just these little comments during rehearsals. And they'll show me emails or notes that supposedly explain it all away, but... I mean, I know what's going on. \n\nIt's like when the violas suddenly decide to sit further back. Which, by the way, completely ruins the acoustics. I actually spent a huge chunk of grad school focusing specifically on spatial acoustics and resonance. The hall we rehearse in right now has this terrible reverb anyway, especially near the HVAC vents on the east wall. The building manager told me he’d fix those vents last October, but he never did. I think he just doesn't care about the space, honestly. I've tried telling him that the temperature fluctuations knock the woodwinds out of tune, and he just looks at me blankly. But... anyway, yeah, the ensemble members, they just keep doing these little things to sabotage the pieces I write, and I can't shake it.",
