    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever heard voices, sounds, or seen things that other people couldn't see or hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, no, nothing like that. I don't hear imaginary voices or see things that aren't there. Though, to be fair, I do hear things other people don't, but that's just because I have perfect pitch. It's actually a bit of a curse sometimes. \n\nLike, just yesterday I was at the coffee shop near the conservatory, and their espresso machine has this high-pitched whine that sits exactly a quarter-tone sharp of B flat. It's excruciating. I tried to tell the barista that her pressure valve was probably wearing out—you can always tell by the frequency shift when the seal gets loose—but she just gave me this totally blank stare. It's impossible to sit in there and review a score with that constant dissonant hum in the background. It honestly amazes me how people can just tune out their sonic environment like that. Most people just walk around with earbuds in anyway, listening to heavily compressed audio files that completely destroy the dynamic range of a recording, so I guess they don't notice. \n\nBut... wait, I'm sorry, what were you asking me? Oh, right. No, no voices or anything like that. Just the music and, well, the espresso machines.",
