    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Outside of your ensemble, do you feel that other people in your life, such as friends or family, are also working against you or untrustworthy?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, no, it's really just the people in the ensemble. My friends and family are fine. I mean, my parents don't always get what I do, but they're supportive. They actually came out for the premiere of that big commission I mentioned. My mom insisted on taking us all out to dinner afterward at this Italian place downtown. \n\nWhich, by the way, was a disaster acoustically. They had these hard tile floors and bare brick walls, and the ambient noise level was easily pushing 80 decibels. You literally couldn't hear the person sitting across from you without shouting. I don't understand why restaurant designers don't incorporate acoustic panels or at least some soft furnishings. It completely ruins the dining experience when all you can hear is the clatter of silverware bouncing off the ceiling. I actually drew up a little sketch on my napkin of how they could install some baffles near the ceiling to absorb the sound, but I obviously didn't give it to the manager. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, my family is fine. They're not trying to sabotage me or anything. It's just the ensemble.",
